{%- case gem_handle -%}

  {%- when 'navratana' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--navratana">
    <h2>What Navratna Is Not</h2>
    <p>Not a Collection of Independent Remedies</p>
    <p>Navratna is not nine separate astrological gemstones worn for nine separate purposes.</p>
    <p>Nor is it simply a jewellery design containing multiple coloured stones.</p>
    <p>Its significance comes from the relationship between the gemstones and the balance they are traditionally believed to create together.</p>
    <p>The value of Navratna lies not in any single gemstone.</p>
    <p>It lies in the harmony of all nine.</p>
   
  </div>

  {%- when 'upratnas' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--upratnas">
    <h2>What Upratnas Are Not</h2>
    <b>Not a Fake, Not a Compromise</b>
    <ul>
      <li>[Placeholder] They are not inferior — they are intentional. Upratnas carry genuine planetary resonance and are recognised in classical Vedic texts.</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] They are not a workaround for those who "cannot afford" the primary stone — they are a valid astrological choice in their own right.</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] They are not interchangeable with any random semiprecious stone — only classically sanctioned substitutes belong here.</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] They are not for everyone in all situations — for serious astrological conditions, the primary gem may still be the right path.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  {%- else -%}
  <div class="gem-tab">
    <p>[Placeholder] Content coming soon.</p>
  </div>

{%- endcase -%}
